<article class="env-lemma" id="02Q9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02Q9">Lemma <span data-tag="02Q9">42.68.39</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian local domain of dimension $1$ with fraction field $K$. For $x \in K \setminus \{ 0, 1\} $ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  d_ A(x, 1 -x) = 1  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $x = a/b$ with $a, b \in A$. The hypothesis implies, since $1 - x = (b - a)/b$, that also $b - a \not= 0$. Hence we compute 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  d_ A(x, 1 - x) = d_ A(a, b - a)d_ A(a, b)^{-1}d_ A(b, b - a)^{-1}d_ A(b, b)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Thus we have to show that $d_ A(a, b - a) d_ A(b, b) = d_ A(b, b - a) d_ A(a, b)$. This is Lemma <a href="/tag/02Q8" data-tag="02Q8">42.68.38</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>